w only for one and i actually want  to  semi-debunk this so first of all  caloric needs don't actually double in  pregnancy  though i get that it can feel like they  must  but even in the third trimester you're  only looking at an  extra 350 to 500 calories  that's literally like a coffee shop  muffin meanwhile depending on your  breast milk supply  most nursing or pumping moms are  expending an extra 500 calories or  more per day so in reality your needs  postpartum for milk production  and recovery are potentially much  greater than they were when you were  growing  that babe inside you let's see what  she's having for dinner usually i'm  having dinner around  6 pm my friends called the early word  special or  granny's delight but also i just feel  better when i eat early and then that  way  later if i'm gonna have like a little  snack i can have something light but i  don't feel like i'm heavy when i go to  bed  love me a granny delight come on if  you're not even eligible for the early  bird special at ihop  are you even momming  but no even though talking about feeling  heavy  when you go to bed sounds kind of like a  diet culture statement  i do get what she's trying to say here i  think a lot of people find that they  have a hard time digesting a big meal  and then just like laying down for bed i  know that i  have found that having like a geriatric  hour meal and then  going for like a slow walk on the  treadmill or outside after dinner  definitely helps with my digestion and  quality of sleep  and ashley and i are not alone but we  had  lamb stew every night and it is  unbelievable lamb purple potatoes whole  garlic  and then he puts it in the oven it's  super delicious super filling and  especially after you have a baby they  say to eat lots of like  really hot nutritional food oh man  i am here for the hearty postpartum  stews  i made a huge batch of like a dozen  different soups and stews before baby o  came so that i had lots of warm  hydrating meals ready to go and i'm just  now coming to the end of my stash sadly  i want some more but i love that the  stew has the protein from the lamb  carbs and the potatoes and i assume  there's like some tomatoes or some other  kind of veg in there  but a stew is also an awesome place to  sneak in a lot of  random leftover pieces of vegetables  that you have in the fridge  so if it was my pot of deliciousness i  would probably throw in some diced  zucchini  some bell peppers and maybe like some  frozen spinach  he'll make this thing called general  chicken because it's literally just  general chicken on the stove top with  garlic salt and pepper  okay i don't know who needs to hear this  probably not my vegan followers  but i just want to say that i think the  best chicken recipes  are the simplest chicken recipes my  hubby tells everyone that i make the  best chicken breast and it's true  i do but really you just want to season  it really well and  not overcook it as far as i'm concerned  those are the only  secrets you need to know on thursday  nights justin and i do date night  because you know  to have a happy marriage you do day  nights  i will treat myself to two tequilas two  margaritas oh  margarita i knew i liked this girl ugh i  haven't had a good margarita in almost  two years because i've either been  pregnant cooped up inside during a  pandemic or  both but it's definitely up there in  my top 20 cocktails  wait a minute what i like a lot of  drinks  now as for the elephant in the room can  you drink  and breastfeed well this is a  complicated and  slightly controversial topic but in  short  you do not need to pump and dump  after hitting the bottle puffing and  dumping doesn't speed up the elimination  of alcohol from the milk  and the amount that finds its way into  breast milk is also  relatively low according to the american  academy of pediatrics section on  breastfeeding  alcoholic beverages should be limited to  no more than  .5 grams of alcohol per kilogram of body  weight  which for a 60 kilogram mother is  approximately  two ounces of liquor eight ounces of  wine or two beers  it's also important to note that alcohol  levels in breast milk peak around  30 to 60 minutes after consumption and  as your blood alcohol level returns to  normal  so too does your milk so most  authorities suggest that if you're sober  enough to drive  you're sober enough to breastfeed  according to the godfather of  breastfeeding  dr newman the biggest risk of drinking  and breastfeeding  is that you might get so drunk you fall  asleep with the baby  or you drop the baby that said this is  not  i repeat not an endorsement to drink  while breastfeeding  i'm just stating the little research and  recommendations that we do have around  this  you have to do what you feel comfortable  with and if that is complete  abstinence then that's great for you too  but i like ashley enjoy a well-timed  drinky drink after the babies  go to bed let's see what else she's  eating we go to alamar usually which is  my favorite local restaurant in dumbo  and i always get the bronzino fillet  with a side of broccoli  and i start with the endive salad i'm  not gonna lie  i do order it out like probably three  times a week  it's amazing that does sound like a  killer meal again there's no harm in  adding like a carb side dish  but if you prefer your carbs in  liquefied grape form  or dessert then i guess that works in my  books  as well so for a restaurant meal this  sounds both delicious  and really nutrient dense so big thumbs  up from me  my favorite food city has to be calabria  italy so my absolute favorite thing to  eat  is the cannolis now i invented my own  way of eating the cannoli for breakfast  and i was putting it on  watermelon call me crazy but it was  like a miracle of explosions in my mouth  i just want to know what all my italian  friends  think about this combo  i mean i get pretty excited about unique  food combinations  like i'm not a purist by any means and  i'm trying to envision it i am trying to  imagine it  and i'm not gonna yuck someone's yum  here because my goodness  she is selling it i honestly i would eat  anything  if it was described first by ashley  graham but my culinary intuition tells  me that  the watermelon would just like sog up  the crisp cookie shell it would be like  dunking a biscotti in  fruity herbal tea instead of coffee that  would just be  such an injustice also i do hope that  she's able to tolerate  some gluten in her diet because i feel  like all the best  pastries and pasta in italy are probably  not gluten free  i have some me time  so that's usually when i'll either pull  out my frozen dark  chocolate out of my freezer because i  think that dark chocolate frozen is the  best  and one of my favorite things to eat is  sliced  apples drizzled with peanut butter on  top  okay so the way i read these interviews  often comes down to  language intention and attitude and  these late night snacks could come  across as super restrictive  as it did when like kelly ripa talked  about her  treats being like a single chocolate  almond  but it really comes down to the context  of one's day and also how they  view that snack ashley talks about these  foods with  absolute enthusiasm and gusto like she  really makes it a sensory experience  just to hear her describe them and while  dark chocolate may be the stereotypical  healthy treat and wellness culture  ashley doesn't seem to discriminate  against classic like 7-eleven special  peanut m  m so it's clear to me that the girl just  probably eats  what she likes and isn't judging herself  for it so  these sound like awesome bedtime snacks  to me  all in i'm loving that i'm seeing a lot  of variety in ashley's diet  with the exception of some potential  restrictions around gluten  and dairy which she may have her own  health reasons for  i don't think that her diet is  particularly restrictive in any way  i mean she puts battery spread on her  bread and eats potatoes in her stew  and knows her way around a bag of cheap  candy  and on that note that is all that i have  for you guys today a big thank you again  to buildbar for sponsoring this video  if you liked it be sure to give it the  thumbs up  leave me a comment below with any other  youtubers or celebrities whose diet you  want me to review  subscribe to the channel and i'll see  you next time on abby's kitchen  bye  [Music]  good
 

